  "name": "24 HR URINARY DOPAMINE ELISA",
  "code": "1077",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"130\" data-end=\"311\">The <strong data-start=\"134\" data-end=\"167\">24-hour urinary dopamine test</strong> measures the total amount of <strong data-start=\"197\" data-end=\"209\">dopamine</strong>, a catecholamine neurotransmitter, excreted in urine over a full day. This test is primarily used to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"313\" data-end=\"652\">\n<li data-start=\"313\" data-end=\"383\">\n<p data-start=\"315\" data-end=\"383\"><strong data-start=\"315\" data-end=\"383\">Evaluate adrenal medulla and sympathetic nervous system function</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"384\" data-end=\"490\">\n<p data-start=\"386\" data-end=\"490\">Monitor or diagnose <strong data-start=\"406\" data-end=\"426\">pheochromocytoma</strong>, <strong data-start=\"428\" data-end=\"445\">neuroblastoma</strong>, or other <strong data-start=\"456\" data-end=\"490\">catecholamine-secreting tumors</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"491\" data-end=\"568\">\n<p data-start=\"493\" data-end=\"568\">Investigate causes of <strong data-start=\"515\" data-end=\"531\">hypertension</strong>, especially if episodic or resistant</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"569\" data-end=\"652\">\n<p data-start=\"571\" data-end=\"652\">Study <strong data-start=\"577\" data-end=\"600\">dopamine metabolism</strong> in certain metabolic or neuropsychiatric conditions</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"654\" data-end=\"796\">Dopamine is a precursor to norepinephrine and epinephrine and plays roles in cardiovascular regulation, renal function, and neurotransmission.</p>\n<p data-start=\"654\" data-end=\"796\">Elevated 24-hour urinary dopamine levels may indicate:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Condition</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Explanation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Pheochromocytoma or paraganglioma</strong></td>\n<td>Tumors of the adrenal medulla or sympathetic chain that secrete catecholamines</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Neuroblastoma</strong></td>\n<td>Malignant tumor common in children, often secreting dopamine</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Stress or acute illness</strong></td>\n<td>May transiently raise catecholamine levels, including dopamine</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Use of certain medications</strong></td>\n<td>E.g., levodopa, MAO inhibitors, amphetamines, which increase dopamine levels</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Hypertensive crisis or autonomic dysregulation</strong></td>\n<td>Seen in rare syndromes or acute states</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"654\" data-end=\"796\">&nbsp;</p>",
